---
description: How to fix a production incident in this repository. Applies to interactive Cursor sessions and to Mender runs.
alwaysApply: false
---
When fixing a production incident:

- Reproduce first. Add one new test under tests/ that fails for the same reason as the incident, before changing any source file.
- Fix the root cause with the smallest change. Docstrings and existing tests define intended behaviour.
- Never hide an error. No bare `except`, no `except Exception`, no skip or xfail markers, no silent defaults.
- Never edit or delete an existing test to make a change pass.
- Do not touch CI, infrastructure, migrations or dependency files as part of an incident fix.
- If intended behaviour cannot be determined from the code, change nothing and say what decision is needed.
